# Pipeline framework

Before changing ingest, Timeline, place locate/upsert, visits, jobs, or workers, read and follow:

**[docs/pipeline-framework-design.md](docs/pipeline-framework-design.md)**

That doc is the source of truth. Do not invent a parallel architecture.

## Hard rules (summary)

- Pipelines compose steps; steps do one job; the runner only logs/retries/records failure stages.
- Prefer **generic** steps (extract, locate, dedupe, upsert). Platform steps only when the API/media requires it.
- **Persona** logic (URL discovery, Timeline gates, link-post vs create-visit) stays **outside** pipelines — no `if timeline` inside shared steps.
- **No overloaded fields** — one intent per field (`source` ≠ review state; do not pack stats into `post_id` / notes).
- Shared steps return **explicit outcomes**; policy at the edge.
- Contextual names; keep the framework small (no plugin/DAG framework).
- `server/` remains a thin adapter — no place/visit business logic in workers beyond calling the library.
- New product behavior uses `travelplanner/features.py` (`enabled(FLAG)`, default off) — no ad-hoc env feature checks. See AGENTS.md § Feature flags.

Use the checklist at the end of the design doc in your change summary.
